STRING CONVERSION — SHORT NOTES

String.valueOf() can convert primitive values and objects into a String.

String.valueOf()
    ↓
Converts a value into String format.


Primitive → String

int     → String
double  → String
float   → String
long    → String
char    → String
boolean → String
short   → String
byte    → String


Examples:

int a = 10;
String s1 = String.valueOf(a);

double b = 10.5;
String s2 = String.valueOf(b);

char c = 'A';
String s3 = String.valueOf(c);

boolean d = true;
String s4 = String.valueOf(d);


Important:

String.valueOf(10)
        ↓
"10"       // String


String.valueOf(true)
        ↓
"true"     // String


String.valueOf('A')
        ↓
"A"        // String